{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Restaurant Rating Prediction - Model Training and Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook covers the model training and evaluation steps for the Restaurant Rating Prediction project.\n",
    "We will:\n",
    "1. Load the dataset\n",
    "2. Perform feature engineering\n",
    "3. Preprocess the data\n",
    "4. Split into training and testing sets\n",
    "5. Train multiple regression models\n",
    "6. Perform hyperparameter tuning on the best model\n",
    "7. Evaluate the tuned model\n",
    "8. Analyze feature importance and explainability\n",
    "9. Save the model and preprocessing pipeline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Import necessary libraries\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Import custom modules\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), '..'))\n",
    "from data.load_data import load_dataset, validate_dataset\n",
    "from features.feature_engineering import engineer_features\n",
    "from preprocessing.preprocessor import preprocess_data\n",
    "from models.train_model import train_models, hyperparameter_tuning, save_model\n",
    "\n",
    "# For modeling\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error, r2_score\n",
    "\n",
    "# For explainability\n",
    "import shap\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set random seed for reproducibility\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set plotting style\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8')\n",
    "sns.set_palette(\"husl\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# For better display in notebooks\n",
    "%matplotlib inline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load the dataset\n",
    "df = load_dataset()\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset shape: {df.shape}\")\n",
    "if validate_dataset(df):\n",
    "    print(\"Dataset validation passed.\")\n    else:\n",
    "    print(\"Dataset validation failed.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Feature Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "We will engineer features as defined in the feature engineering module."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Engineer features\n",
    "df_engineered = engineer_features(df)\n",
    "print(f\"Original shape: {df.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Engineered shape: {df_engineered.shape}\")\n",
    "df_engineered.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Data Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "We will separate the target variable and preprocess the features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Separate features and target\n",
    "X = df_engineered.drop('Aggregate rating', axis=1)\n",
    "y = df_engineered['Aggregate rating']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Features shape: {X.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Target shape: {y.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Preprocess the data\n",
    "X_processed, preprocessor = preprocess_data(X)\n",
    "print(f\"Processed features shape: {X_processed.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Train-Test Split\n",
    "\n",
    "We will split the data into training and testing sets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Split the data\n",
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X_processed, y, test_size=0.2, random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(f\"Training set shape: {X_train.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test set shape: {X_test.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Train Multiple Models\n",
    "\n",
    "We will train and compare multiple regression models."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train models\n",
    "results = train_models(X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a summary DataFrame for comparison\n",
    "summary = []\n",
    "for name, res in results.items():\n",
    "    summary.append({\n",
    "        'Model': name,\n",
    "        'Test MAE': res['test_mae'],\n",
    "        'Test RMSE': res['test_rmse'],\n",
    "        'Test R2': res['test_r2'],\n",
    "        'CV MAE': res['cv_mae']\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "summary_df = pd.DataFrame(summary)\n",
    "summary_df = summary_df.sort_values('Test MAE')\n",
    "display(summary_df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Hyperparameter Tuning\n",
    "\n",
    "We will tune the hyperparameters of the best performing model (based on Test MAE)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Identify the best model based on Test MAE\n",
    "best_model_name = summary_df.iloc[0]['Model']\n",
    "print(f\"Best model based on Test MAE: {best_model_name}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get the base model instance\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeRegressor\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestRegressor, GradientBoostingRegressor\n",
    "from xgboost import XGBRegressor\n",
    "\n",
    "base_models = {\n",
    "    'Linear Regression': LinearRegression(),\n",
    "    'Decision Tree': DecisionTreeRegressor(random_state=42),\n",
    "    'Random Forest': RandomForestRegressor(random_state=42, n_estimators=100),\n",
    "    'Gradient Boosting': GradientBoostingRegressor(random_state=42, n_estimators=100),\n",
    "    'XGBoost': XGBRegressor(random_state=42, n_estimators=100)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "base_model = base_models[best_model_name]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define parameter grids for each model\n",
    "param_grids = {\n",
    "    'Linear Regression': {},  # No hyperparameters to tune\n",
    "    'Decision Tree': {\n",
    "        'max_depth': [5, 10, 15, 20, None],\n",
    "        'min_samples_split': [2, 5, 10],\n",
    "        'min_samples_leaf': [1, 2, 4]\n",
    "    },\n    "    'Random Forest': {\n",
    "        'n_estimators': [50, 100, 200],\n",
    "        'max_depth': [5, 10, 15, None],\n",
    "        'min_samples_split': [2, 5, 10],\n",
    "        'min_samples_leaf': [1, 2, 4]\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'Gradient Boosting': {\n",
    "        'n_estimators': [50, 100, 200],\n",
    "        'learning_rate': [0.01, 0.1, 0.2],\n",
    "        'max_depth': [3, 5, 7],\n",
    "        'min_samples_split': [2, 5, 10],\n",
    "        'min_samples_leaf': [1, 2, 4]\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'XGBoost': {\n",
    "        'n_estimators': [50, 100, 200],\n",
    "        'learning_rate': [0.01, 0.1, 0.2],\n",
    "        'max_depth': [3, 5, 7],\n",
    "        'min_samples_split': [2, 5, 10],\n",
    "        'min_samples_leaf': [1, 2, 4]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get parameter grid for the best model\n",
    "param_grid = param_grids[best_model_name]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Perform hyperparameter tuning (using RandomizedSearchCV for efficiency)\n",
    "if param_grid:  # Only tune if there are parameters to tune\n",
    "    print(f\"Performing hyperparameter tuning for {best_model_name}...\")\n",
    "    tuned_model = hyperparameter_tuning(base_model, param_grid, X_train, y_train, method='random', n_iter=10)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"{best_model_name} has no hyperparameters to tune. Using base model.\")\n",
    "    tuned_model = base_model\n",
    "\n",
    "# Evaluate the tuned model on the test set\n",
    "y_pred_tuned = tuned_model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "tuned_mae = mean_absolute_error(y_test, y_pred_tuned)\n",
    "tuned_mse = mean_squared_error(y_test, y_pred_tuned)\n",
    "tuned_rmse = np.sqrt(tuned_mse)\n",
    "tuned_r2 = r2_score(y_test, y_pred_tuned)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Tuned {best_model_name} - Test MAE: {tuned_mae:.4f}, Test RMSE: {tuned_rmse:.4f}, Test R2: {tuned_r2:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Feature Importance and Explainability\n",
    "\n",
    "We will analyze the feature importance of the tuned model and use SHAP for explainability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Get feature names after preprocessing\n",
    "# We need to get the feature names from the preprocessor\n",
    "# For simplicity, we'll get the feature names from the engineered data before preprocessing\n",
    "# Note: After one-hot encoding, the feature names change. We'll get them from the preprocessor.\n",
    "# Let's create a function to get feature names after preprocessing\n",
    "def get_feature_names(preprocessor):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Get feature names after column transformation.\"\"\"\n",
    "    feature_names = []\n",
    "    for name, trans, cols in preprocessor.transformers_:\n",
    "        if trans == 'passthrough':\n",
    "            feature_names.extend(cols)\n",
    "        elif hasattr(trans, 'get_feature_names_out'):\n",
    "            feature_names.extend(trans.get_feature_names_out(cols))\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            # For transformers that don't have get_feature_names_out (like imputer+scaler in a pipeline)\n",
    "            # We'll use the original column names for numerical passthrough after scaling\n",
    "            # This is a simplification; in practice, you might need to handle pipelines.\n",
    "            feature_names.extend(cols)\n",
    "    return feature_names\n",
    "\n",
    "# Try to get feature names\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    feature_names = get_feature_names(preprocessor)\n",
    "    print(f\"Number of features after preprocessing: {len(feature_names)}\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Could not get feature names from preprocessor: {e}\")\n",
    "    # Fallback to using the engineered feature names\n",
    "    feature_names = X.columns.tolist()\n",
    "    print(f\"Using engineered feature names: {len(feature_names)} features\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# For tree-based models, we can get feature importance\n",
    "if hasattr(tuned_model, 'feature_importances_'):\n",
    "    importances = tuned_model.feature_importances_\n",
    "    # Sort features by importance\n",
    "    indices = np.argsort(importances)[::-1]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Plot feature importance\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\n",
    "    plt.title(f\"Feature Importances ({best_model_name})\")\n",
    "    plt.bar(range(len(importances)), importances[indices], align=\"center\")\n",
    "    plt.xticks(range(len(importances)), [feature_names[i] for i in indices], rotation=90)\n",
    "    plt.xlim([-1, len(importances)])\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Print top 10 features\n",
    "    print(\"Top 10 important features:\")\n",
    "    for i in range(min(10, len(feature_names))):\n",
    "        print(f\"{feature_names[indices[i]]}: {importances[indices[i]]:.4f}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"{best_model_name} does not have feature_importances_ attribute.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## SHAP Explainability\n",
    "\n",
    "We will use SHAP to explain the model's predictions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize SHAP explainer\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    if best_model_name in ['Random Forest', 'Gradient Boosting', 'XGBoost', 'Decision Tree']:\n",
    "        explainer = shap.TreeExplainer(tuned_model)\n",
    "    elif best_model_name == 'Linear Regression':\n",
    "        explainer = shap.LinearExplainer(tuned_model, X_train)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        explainer = shap.Explainer(tuned_model, X_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Calculate SHAP values for a subset of the test set (for efficiency)\n",
    "    X_test_shap = X_test[:min(100, len(X_test))]  # Limit to 100 samples\n",
    "    shap_values = explainer.shap_values(X_test_shap)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Plot SHAP summary\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\n",
    "    shap.summary_plot(shap_values, X_test_shap, feature_names=feature_names, plot_type=\"bar\")\n",
    "    plt.title(\"SHAP Feature Importance (Bar)\")\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # SHAP summary plot\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\n",
    "    shap.summary_plot(shap_values, X_test_shap, feature_names=feature_names)\n",
    "    plt.title(\"SHAP Summary Plot\")\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "    \n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Could not compute SHAP values: {e}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Actual vs Predicted Plot\n",
    "\n",
    "We will create a scatter plot of actual vs predicted values for the tuned model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Actual vs Predicted\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "plt.scatter(y_test, y_pred_tuned, alpha=0.6)\n",
    "plt.plot([y_test.min(), y_test.max()], [y_test.min(), y_test.max()], 'r--', lw=2)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Actual Aggregate Rating')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Predicted Aggregate Rating')\n",
    "plt.title('Actual vs Predicted Ratings (Tuned Model)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Residual Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "We will analyze the residuals of the tuned model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Residuals\n",
    "residuals = y_test - y_pred_tuned\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\n",
    "plt.scatter(y_pred_tuned, residuals, alpha=0.6)\n",
    "plt.axhline(y=0, color='r', linestyle='--')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Predicted Aggregate Rating')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Residuals')\n",
    "plt.title('Residuals vs Predicted Values')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\n",
    "sns.histplot(residuals, kde=True)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Residuals')\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of Residuals')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Mean residual: {np.mean(residuals):.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Standard deviation of residuals: {np.std(residuals):.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Save Model and Artifacts\n",
    "\n",
    "We will save the tuned model, preprocessor, and feature names for deployment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Save the tuned model, preprocessor, and feature names\n",
    "save_model(tuned_model, preprocessor, feature_names)\n",
    "print(\"Model and artifacts saved successfully.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "We have completed the model training and evaluation process. Key steps:\n",
    "1. Loaded and engineered features from the dataset\n",
    "2. Preprocessed the data using a scikit-learn pipeline\n",
    "3. Trained and compared multiple regression models\n",
    "4. Performed hyperparameter tuning on the best model\n",
    "5. Evaluated the tuned model using MAE, RMSE, R2, and residual analysis\n",
    "6. Analyzed feature importance and explainability using SHAP\n",
    "7. Saved the model and preprocessing artifacts for deployment\n",
    "\n",
    "The tuned model is now ready for use in prediction applications."
   ]
  }
 ],
